  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-03-05T02:21:00.030Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Phys Bone's Safty Setting does not have a self-defense feature to the \"Limit Dynamic Bone Usage\" that once existed in Dynamic Bone.\nThus, it is not possible to hide avatars that contain an excessive number of Phys Bones.\nWhat this means is that users with a low CPU environment (especially Meta Quest) may get very low FPS and a poor VR experience.\nTherefore, I request that either an option be revived to allow users to set Phys Bone limits for both themselves and others, or that a checkbox be added to toggle the component active/disable completely.\n(It seems possible to display the avatar as a FallBack avatar in excess of \"Bones\", \"Physics Collider\" and \"Physics Rigitbodies\", due to Avatar Performance Limitations.)",
